{"command": "cat /testbed/.specify/memory/constitution.md", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "# TinyDB Constitution\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\nAll changes to TinyDB MUST maintain backward compatibility with the existing public API. No public method, class, or function signature may be altered in a way that breaks existing user code. Any API modification requires explicit justification and migration documentation.\n\n### II. Attach Testable Acceptance Criteria to Requirements\nEvery requirement MUST include testable acceptance criteria. Requirements without clear, verifiable test conditions are incomplete. Tests must cover happy paths, edge cases, and error conditions before implementation begins.\n\n### III. Distinguish Observed Evidence from Unverified Assertions\nDevelopment decisions MUST be grounded in observed evidence, not assumptions. Performance claims, bug reproductions, and behavior descriptions require measurable data or reproducible test cases. Unverified assertions must be explicitly flagged as such.\n\n### IV. Prefer Simple Scoped Implementations\nSolutions MUST favor simplicity and narrow scope over generality. Implementations should address the specific problem at hand without over-engineering. Complexity must be justified and documented. YAGNI principles apply.\n\n### V. Document Unresolved Assumptions and Regressions\nAll development artifacts MUST include explicit documentation of unresolved assumptions, known limitations, and any regressions introduced. This documentation must be visible to reviewers and future maintainers.\n\n## Development Standards\n\nTinyDB is a lightweight, document-oriented database. All contributions must align with its design philosophy: minimalism, simplicity, and ease of use. Third-party dependencies are minimized. The codebase targets Python 3.10+ with type annotations.\n\n## Review Process\n\nAll changes must pass existing tests and adhere to the coding standards defined in this constitution. Code reviews must verify compliance with each principle. Complexity claims require justification.\n\n## Governance\n\nThis constitution supersedes all other development practices within the TinyDB project. Amendments require documentation of the change, rationale, and migration plan if applicable. All contributors must acknowledge these principles.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-09-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-09-17\n"}